.TH AVR\-REPO\-LIST 1 "" "avr 0.1.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-repo-list \- List repositories you can access in an organization.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr repo list
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List repositories you can access in an organization.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr repo list
    avr repo list --json full_name,repository_id
    avr repo list --json '*' -q '.[].full_name'
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    full_name, platform, platform_repository_id, repository_id
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Max repositories to return. (default: 100)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-repo (1)
